WEBVTT

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:14.860
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.070
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.990
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:43.990
<b>Chapter Four          The Rainbow-Colored Past</b>

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.850
Nishinosono-kun...

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.430
He's still warm.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.090
Is he dead?

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:05.940
Yes.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.410
It's broken.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:10.060
The radio... Did the killer break it?

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.770
In other words, the police 
haven't been contacted yet.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.530
Who did this?

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:19.140
Are you okay?

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.450
This is a murder!

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.650
Stabbing yourself in that area is impossible.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.620
He must have known his killer.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.730
He was stabbed in the back of the neck,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.530
so he knew the killer had gotten in behind him,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.470
and he turned his back on the murderer.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.960
Nishinosono-kun...

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.890
It hasn't been long since he was killed, right?

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.120
Which means that, after they killed Director Shindo,

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.430
they escaped via that entrance,

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.410
not the elevator we came up.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:45.340
Therefore,

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.810
the killer is still inside the lab.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:57.690
The director, too?

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.440
Shimada-kun, see who opened 
the door on the roof.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.650
O-Okay.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.050
How's his wife doing?

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.450
I gave her a tranquilizer.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.580
And Miki-san, too.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.110
You shouldn't stare at it like that.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.120
Purple...

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.120
A very important...

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.250
It's important?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.330
Nishinosono-kun, let's get out of here.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.650
It would be dangerous to get any more involved.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.890
I'm fine.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.530
I want to know the truth!

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.260
About what?

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.640
About why this happened.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:08.850
Here it is.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:13.030
The last person to open the door was Yamane-san.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.000
At 2:40... Just now.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.560
Before that?

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.730
Before that, it was also you.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:20.890
1:43...

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:23.200
Not that door... The other one!

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.750
It was Mochizuki-san.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.270
1:44.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.950
Yesterday morning was the last time before then.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.370
But that's impossible!

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.000
We have no proof that Deborah is perfect!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.630
Many strange things have been happening.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.220
So what?

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.920
Don't be illogical!

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:45.880
I'm sorry...

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.680
There may be

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:51.010
clues left in the doctor's rooms.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.600
Yamane Yukihiro.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.500
How do you open this door from the inside?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.320
Dr. Magata does the same thing he just did.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.880
Deborah, leave the door as it is.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.020
<i>Understood.</i>

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:18.670
Be careful, okay?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.400
Why did she need this room,

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.770
when she never had guests?

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.720
It's strange...

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:33.680
There isn't a single book on her research subjects.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:37.650
Let's split up and search for clues.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.240
Is this the doctor's office?

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.190
Probably.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.300
I've never been in here, either,

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.320
so I can't say for sure.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.280
Metal powder...

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.150
What was she making here?

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.050
Did the doctor watch TV?

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.570
I don't know.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:15.060
I never heard her mention it.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.310
Two of them.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.490
It's very clean.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.320
Maybe she liked things clean.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.520
Maybe.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.990
She did all this by herself.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.970
This is the last room.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.190
I believe it's her bedroom.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.540
It's locked...

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.830
Locked? Why?

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:44.800
It's locked from the inside.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.130
Get back.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.110
Hey, is anyone in there?

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.040
Who's there?

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.800
Be quiet! I heard a voice.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.400
Who's there?

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.190
That's Dr. Magata's voice...

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.530
What?! That's impossible!

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:11.280
It's me, Yamane! Open the door, please!

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.830
Are you Dr. Magata?

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.500
Who's there?

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:31.040
Is someone in there?

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.620
Who's there?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.470
What?

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.100
Who are you?

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.770
I am Michiru.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.050
Is this what she was making?

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.080
Blocks?

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.440
She bought these years ago.

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:02.430
I remember putting them in the mail slot.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.960
Did she like stuffed animals?

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.430
I don't know...

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:13.720
Michiru?

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.830
Yes, I am Michiru.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:17.930
Where is Dr. Magata?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.650
Dr. Magata?

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.340
What happened to her?

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:23.510
What happened?

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:25.350
This isn't going to work.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.270
Did this robot lock the door?

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.980
If it can unlock the door, it can lock it.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:33.430
Michiru, lock the door.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:34.910
Understood.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.750
Pretty impressive.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.890
There's an infrared sensor on the hand.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.930
That's how it judges the distance to the door.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:58.760
It's emitting lasers from there to judge its position.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.360
It emits lasers in four directors,

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.210
and then looks at reflections from the walls.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.980
You're amazing, Sensei.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.680
It can lock and unlock the door,

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.770
but it can't open it.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.670
Why did she make a robot like this?

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.240
I don't know. To kill time?

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.560
Nobody's here.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.070
There was never a chance there would be.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:22.310
But the killer must be somewhere.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:24.640
Two people are dead.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:27.040
This place is too clean, though.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.880
It's hard to believe something 
awful happened here.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:32.180
What are you trying to say, Sensei?

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.230
Merely what I'm feeling.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.530
We never found anything...

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:41.220
No killer, no weapon, and not 
the doctor's limbs, either.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.190
How does she dispose of garbage?

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.260
She creates some trash every day, right?

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.790
There should be a trash chute somewhere...

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:50.230
It was in the kitchen.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.930
Then you couldn't throw away anything big?

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:57.970
No, you could.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.760
If you chopped it up into pieces.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:02.990
Nishinosono-kun,

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.490
are you remotely familiar with 
the concept of "delicacy"?

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.900
Don't make fun of me. That's a delicious dish, right?

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:12.540
Tell me what you think about this, please.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.750
There still isn't enough information.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.590
That's no help.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:23.660
After murdering the doctor, the killer 
severed her limbs in the bathroom,

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:25.640
and threw them down the trash chute.

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.540
Then the killer thoroughly cleaned the room.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:34.150
Which means the killer was 
here for quite a long time.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:37.010
But the killer was just on the roof.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.500
You went up there, didn't you?

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:41.690
Yes.

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.720
When the doctor's sister, Miki-san, arrived,

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.410
Director Shindo was alive.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.970
And the next time you went up there, he was dead.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.400
That was only thirty minutes or so.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.130
How did the killer get up to the roof?

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.400
Or were they on the roof the whole time,

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.050
and possibly still there?

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.620
Either way,

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.700
the killer was in this room, dismembering her,

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.240
before going to the roof...

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:11.140
Why did the killer need to do that, anyway?

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.930
What do you think?

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:16.890
Because she was too heavy to 
put on the cart otherwise?

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.700
I don't think so.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:23.280
You really think a person intelligent enough 
to take over the lab's computer system

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.980
would go to all the trouble of severing 
her arms and legs just for that?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.420
You're right.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:31.480
I don't really want to play my 
trump card now, but...

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:33.380
What do you mean by trump card?

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.450
"This isn't my specialty."

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.380
But you can't escape.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.080
We're locked in here,

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:44.180
in this windowless world.

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.320
It's all shut down...

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.110
Boot it up.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.130
Roger.

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.480
May I touch it?

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.480
Go ahead.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:02.240
Look at that!

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.610
Red Magic, version 6!

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.510
Version 6?

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:08.860
The lab's still running version 4.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:12.570
I heard that the doctor was working 
on the next version, but...

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.680
I'm surprised to learn she was up to 6.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.930
It's dated yesterday.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.500
<b>Everything Becomes F</b>

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:22.510
"Everything becomes F."

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.740
"F"? What does that mean?

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.260
Finished?

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:31.220
What's this?

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:37.570
"I have left no trace on my PC that I was alive.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:40.410
I shall warn you of this fact here,

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:42.290
so there's no need to waste time.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:44.900
The same is true of my workstation.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:48.060
However, I shall leave the new compiler

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:50.710
and Red Magic, version 6,

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:54.630
as final presents from me.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.510
— Magata Shiki."

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:01.300
"I was opposed to it, but it seems there's no choice.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.680
It's unfortunate that I must leave Michiru...

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.750
the one who most wanted to leave.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:08.800
This is the sole thing that upsets me.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:12.780
But there's something I have to do.

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:14.530
— Kurimoto Kishio."

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.390
Michiru...

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:18.260
That robot?

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:21.050
"I did all the cleaning.

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.740
I even got rid of the mildew in the bathroom.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.510
I want to see the ocean again, 
for the first time in so long.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.960
Don't mess up my wedding dress, please.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:31.960
— Sasaki Suma"?

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.210
Sasaki Suma?

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:35.570
Who is that?

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:41.100
No, these two, Kurimoto Kishio and 
Sasaki Suma, don't actually exist.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.190
These two are Dr. Magata's...

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:45.400
Other personalities.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.580
I've heard that rumor.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.490
When I met her, she told me the same thing.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.090
That she had multiple personalities.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.900
In other words, she left all these messages?

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:58.560
I don't think so.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.410
From these messages, they must be from the killer.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:06.470
Though I wonder how the killer knew so 
much about her other personalities.

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:10.220
Just as she said, there don't appear 
to be any other files.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:12.720
There's nothing left here, either.

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:15.330
It's past four.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.600
Let's get some sleep.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.190
Yeah, I agree.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.350
You guys must be tired, too.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:23.710
Will you return to the campground?

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:26.280
Do you want to, Nishinosono-kun?

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.230
No.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.710
I want to learn why this happened.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.100
Even if you know, it has nothing to do with you.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:35.100
No.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.310
I feel like I have to know.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:41.910
We'll stay a while longer.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.440
We're witnesses, too.

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:45.940
I understand.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.050
I'll be in my room.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:52.550
Tell me if there's anything you need.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:58.300
By now, it's probably light outside...

00:14:58.300 --> 00:14:59.150
Yeah.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:03.460
In here, it feels like we've 
been abandoned by time.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:07.090
Isn't "released from" a better phrase 
than "abandoned by"?

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:08.500
That's right...

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.650
This is your ideal environment, isn't it?

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.410
No. At the very least, not right now.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.910
Do you think everyone's worried?

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:22.230
Yeah.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:26.610
This is the first time in my life 
I've felt the need for a cell phone.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.000
But for some reason, I...

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:30.480
Purple?

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:33.160
That's what you said, right?

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.930
"A very important..."

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.900
Let's get some rest.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.060
You go ahead.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:45.000
There's a room I wanted to see.

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:49.840
This was her one window, wasn't it?

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.050
I've always wondered...

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:54.340
Wondered what?

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:57.670
Why did she meet with me?

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:03.950
Perhaps she was interested in the 
girl named Nishinosono Moe.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:06.670
Interested how?

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:07.900
I don't know.

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:12.080
But I think that might be it, too.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:16.540
There may have been something 
she wanted to learn from me.

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:23.510
Sensei, what's the thing that 
bothers you most right now?

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.940
When I run out of cigarettes, I'll be very sad.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:30.040
I'm not joking. I'm asking seriously.

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:32.840
"Everything becomes F."

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.210
Because Dr. Magata wrote that?

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:38.450
It doesn't matter who wrote it.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:40.020
You're joking again.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.610
And you, Nishinosono-kun?

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.120
For me...

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.440
It's the wedding dress.

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:48.010
Did she make that?

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.290
There was a sewing machine in her room.

00:16:51.350 --> 00:16:52.110
No.

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:54.560
I asked Hasebe-san,

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.950
and he said she bought it three years ago.

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:58.110
Why?

00:16:58.110 --> 00:16:59.130
No idea.

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:01.220
Maybe she wanted to try it on.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.310
Something that over-the-top?

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:04.610
I refuse to believe that.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:05.750
Huh?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.680
You wore one once, didn't you?

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:09.340
M-Me?

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:13.170
In elementary school, you had an outfit 
with lots of lace around here—

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:16.220
Sensei, don't talk about old stuff like that!

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:20.500
But it was a lot nicer than
 the way you dress now.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.610
Like a cute doll.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:23.880
A doll...

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:28.540
My parents died when I was fourteen.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:31.320
A doll did it.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:34.240
I saw it happen.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.930
A doll killed them.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:39.140
That's what she said, right?

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:43.190
Yeah. And she also talked about 
her multiple personalities.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:45.960
When you say "doll,"

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:49.900
do you mean that your other personality did it?

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:53.940
It is true that there are other 
personalities within me.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:57.510
Not only one. Many.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.860
Many?

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.390
But you see,

00:18:00.680 --> 00:18:02.950
the others inside me

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.520
do not know about my parents.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.270
How can you tell?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:11.950
Because we're always talking.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:13.520
I can tell.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.100
Seven.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.380
Seven?

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:20.380
Out of the numbers from one to ten, 
seven is the only lonely number.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:24.300
"So the only personality

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:27.480
inside me with a motive to kill my parents

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.450
is Magata Shiki.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:32.220
I am the only one that is seven..."

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:36.870
In other words, she is a doll herself.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.270
What does that mean?

00:18:39.650 --> 00:18:41.930
Think about what dolls are, conceptually.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.330
They have no wills of their own,

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:47.220
and sometimes, they're controlled by other people.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.800
<i>Summer, the year 2000.</i>

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.220
<i>I stood atop a hill,</i>

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.700
<i>looking down the long slope.</i>

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.240
<i>I heard her voice.</i>

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:01.700
<i>Or more precisely, their...</i>

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.500
Hey, Suma-san...

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:06.450
You were with him for a while, yes?

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:07.110
Yes.

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:10.330
Did he invite you? Or did you invite him?

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.630
It was I.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:14.880
Do men not find that unattractive?

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:17.150
No, I don't need generalities.

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.960
Wouldn't he find that unattractive?

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:20.640
Yes, probably.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:21.920
I see.

00:19:23.230 --> 00:19:25.100
I'm starting to get nervous.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.920
That's a rare thing for you to say.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:28.600
How are you nervous?

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.910
Without a body, you wouldn't understand.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:32.850
Are you okay, Shiki?

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:35.140
It's my first time, so I'm not very confident.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:36.630
But it's probably all right.

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:38.230
Don't force yourself.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:39.490
What a strange warning.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:42.360
I was merely trying to get you to relax.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:46.270
Kishio, in the short time I haven't 
seen you, you've matured a lot.

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:51.140
It's only humans who take
 this long to become adults.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.830
<i>I said to her,</i>

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:56.870
<i>"You aren't normal."</i>

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:00.100
<i>And she answered,</i>

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.910
<i>"I am not normal."</i>

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:07.370
I have a request.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.060
Put your clothes on.

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:11.460
Touch me...

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:16.020
Please. All you have to do is touch me.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:17.690
Why do I have to—

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:25.340
<i>And I began</i>

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:28.450
<i>to fall down the long slope.</i>

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:33.000
<i>Not knowing where I would go...</i>

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:07.490
Then I shall ask a question.

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:10.950
You lost your parents, did you not?

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.120
Do you remember that day?

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:16.440
Did you cry?

00:21:18.490 --> 00:21:22.350
When it happened, I'm certain there 
was someone next to you.
